 "observations": [
  "The page number «215» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it; at the right the number of the table, «Tab. 100», in bold sans serif, underlined. The page has no signature and no title: the folios of the manuscripts stand at the right above the double rule of the first field, in one line of their own, «C 95r, O 150v, N 61v.», the letters raised (L01).",
  "The page holds three fields, as pp. 206-214 (JP2 0238-0246): «Viginti1) gradus Leonis» (L02), «Viginti quinque3) gradus Leonis» (L14) and «Triginta4) gradus Leonis» (L22), the ascendant at 20°, 25° and 30° of Leo, with the numbers for the sextile, the quadrature and the trine (L03, L15, L23); headings and numbers in bold. The heads of the columns of the first field as on p. 214 (JP2 0246, L05-L08), from Leo to Capricornus, with «Horoscopus» in each, and with note 2 at «Capricorn.», which O wrote over «Aquarius» (L04-L07). The second and the third field have no heads. Double rules divide the fields.",
  "The numbers at the head of a field, as on pp. 206-214 (JP2 0238-0246), are a third, a half and two thirds of the last number of the field: 205° 51′ (L13) gives 68° 37′, 102° 55.5′ and 137° 14′, printed 68° 37′, 102° 55′ and 137° 14′ (L03); 206° 2′ (L21) gives 68° 40.7′, 103° 1′ and 137° 21.3′, printed 68° 41′, 103° 1′ and 137° 21′ (L15); 208° 0′ (L29) gives 69° 20′, 104° 0′ and 138° 40′, as printed (L23).",
  "The columns, as on p. 214 (JP2 0246): in Leo the first field lies within 26′ of the oblique ascensions from the beginning of Leo for the latitude 38° 30′ (computed with the obliquity 23° 35′; 6° 14′, 12° 31′, 18° 48′, 25° 6′, 31° 23′, 37° 39′), the second 6′ to 46′ below them and the third 11′ to 1° 19′ below them; in Virgo the first lies 18′ to 29′ below them, the second from 31′ below to 6′ above them and the third 58′ to 1° 26′ below them; from Libra on all three fall far below them, to 205° 51′, 206° 2′ and 208° 0′ at the end of Capricornus, where the oblique ascension from the beginning of Leo is 214° 10′. The last numbers of the six fields of Leo grow by 2° 32′, 2° 5′, 1° 56′, 11′ and 1° 58′ (199° 18′, 201° 50′ and 203° 55′ on p. 214, JP2 0246, L14, L22, L30; here L13, L21, L29); from the end of Sagittarius on the first field here stands 30′ to 52′ above the mean of the neighbouring fields, the second 32′ to 54′ below it.",
  "Notes on the readings. Checked by the other fields, which differ by 5° of the ascendant, and by the steps of the columns: the edition's readings are the nearer at 10° of Leo in the first field (note a, L09: C's 30 against the 25 of O and N, the steps 6° 5′ and 6° 6′ against 6° 0′ and 6° 11′; the oblique ascension 12° 31′), at 25° of Virgo in the first (note b, L12: O's 68 against C's 78), in the quadrature and the trine of the second (notes c and d, L15: the 103° 1′ and 137° 21′ of O and N, a half and two thirds of 206° 2′, against C's 104° 0′ and 138° 40′, the quadrature and the trine of the third field, L23), at 5° and 10° of Capricornus in the second (notes e and f, L16-L17: the editor's 177 and 182 for the 167 and 172 of all three manuscripts), at 5° of Leo in the third (note g, L24: O's 6 against C's 5, the steps 6° 3′ and 6° 15′ against 5° 3′ and 7° 15′), at 25° of Virgo in the third (note i, L28: C's 28 against O's 18, the steps 5° 56′ and 6° 27′ against 5° 46′ and 6° 37′) and at 30° of Sagittarius in the third (note k, L29: O's 174 against C's 164). At 15° of Virgo in the third field (note h, L26) C's 20 gives the steps 6° 25′ and 6° 12′, the 10 of O and N 6° 15′ and 6° 22′; at 5° of Capricornus in the third (note l, L24) C's 30 gives 5° 15′ and 5° 25′, the 35 of O and N 5° 20′ and 5° 20′; at 15° of Capricornus in the third (note m, L26) the readings differ by 1′; none of these is decided.",
  "The numbers of the notes c and d (N03) end with a point before the bracket and before the siglum C, «103. 1.]», «104. 0. C», «137. 21.]», «138. 40. C»: see the critical note. The dash before the note g (N04) is broken into a short piece of 7 px and a long one of 30 px; written as one dash. «corr. ex.» (N01) in italics, the point of «corr.» set low. A speck at the upper left of the C of «5 C» (N04), and specks in the margins; not transcribed."
